{%- comment -%}
  Group — an invisible flex wrapper. Its only job is to arrange the blocks
  nested inside it in a row or column, with independent mobile and desktop
  direction, alignment, gap and width.

  It is pure layout: no padding, no gutter, no surface, no card presentation.
  A gutter-aware inset, background, border or radius belongs to the card or section
  around it, never here. Alignment is resolved
  through snippets/alignments.liquid; gap through snippets/space-token.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # Height. Auto is the natural content height. Stretch matches the tallest
  # sibling on the flex line (the card contract's Auto/Stretch pair). Fill
  # Parent additionally takes the parent's full height, which only resolves
  # when the parent already has one.
  assign height_mode = block.settings.height_mode | default: 'auto'

  # Vertical placement is one choice with two shapes: Alignment pins the items
  # to one end (or the middle), Spread pushes them apart. Spread overrides the
  # main-axis alignment, so it is emitted after the direction block in each
  # breakpoint.
  assign distribute_css = blank
  if block.settings.align_y_mode == 'spread'
    assign spread = block.settings.spread | default: 'space_between'
    if spread == 'space_around'
      assign distribute_css = 'space-around'
    else
      assign distribute_css = 'space-between'
    endif
  endif

  capture gap_css
    render 'space-token', key: block.settings.gap
  endcapture

  assign row_item_min = block.settings.row_item_min_width | default: 240

  # Width sizing. The merchant picks Auto (Hug / Fill) or Custom (Fixed /
  # Percentage); those two selects resolve here into one internal key so the
  # CSS below stays a single switch. Raw flex values are never exposed.
  assign width_key = 'fill'
  if block.settings.width_mode == 'custom'
    assign width_key = block.settings.width_custom | default: 'percent'
  else
    assign width_key = block.settings.width_auto | default: 'fill'
  endif

  # Percentage widths subtract a share of the parent's gap (--gap-size,
  # inherited) so e.g. two 50% Groups still fit on one line.
  assign pw = block.settings.percent_width | plus: 0
  assign gap_factor = 100 | minus: pw | divided_by: 100.0
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Direction decides which axis each alignment drives: in a row the horizontal
  alignment is the main axis (justify-content) and the vertical one is the
  cross axis (align-items); in a column they swap. Emitted once for the mobile
  base and once for the desktop override (mobile-first, single 768px
  breakpoint), so a Group can be a column on mobile and a row on desktop with
  correct alignment in both.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture layout_css_mobile -%}
  --align-x: var(--align-x-mobile, center);
  --align-y: var(--align-y-mobile, flex-start);
  --text-align: var(--text-align-mobile, center);
  text-align: var(--text-align);
  flex-direction: {{ block.settings.direction_mobile }};
  {%- if block.settings.direction_mobile == 'row' -%}
    flex-wrap: {% if block.settings.wrap %}wrap{% else %}nowrap{% endif %};
    justify-content: var(--align-x);
    align-items: var(--align-y);
  {%- else -%}
    align-items: var(--align-x);
    justify-content: var(--align-y);
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- unless distribute_css == blank -%}
    justify-content: {{ distribute_css }};
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture layout_css_desktop -%}
  --align-x: var(--align-x-desktop, center);
  --align-y: var(--align-y-desktop, flex-start);
  --text-align: var(--text-align-desktop, center);
  text-align: var(--text-align);
  flex-direction: {{ block.settings.direction_desktop }};
  {%- if block.settings.direction_desktop == 'row' -%}
    flex-wrap: {% if block.settings.wrap %}wrap{% else %}nowrap{% endif %};
    justify-content: var(--align-x);
    align-items: var(--align-y);
  {%- else -%}
    align-items: var(--align-x);
    justify-content: var(--align-y);
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- unless distribute_css == blank -%}
    justify-content: {{ distribute_css }};
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{% style %}
  /* Flex group. Mobile-first base + single 768px desktop override. */
  .group--{{ block.id }} {
    {% render 'alignments', source: block.settings %}
    display: flex;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    {%- comment -%}
      SIZING CONTRACT — read this before touching Width or Height below.

      `flex` and `align-self` are axis-RELATIVE: they follow the parent's
      direction, not the page's. In a row parent the main axis is the width and
      `align-self` is the height; in a column parent they swap. So a Width
      setting that emits the `flex` shorthand silently becomes a Height setting
      whenever this Group is nested in a column — which is every Rich Content
      stack. That is exactly how Width Fill (`flex: 1 1 0%`) used to eat all the
      available height while Height Auto sat there emitting nothing, and how
      Width Hug (`flex: 0 0 auto`) appeared to "fix" the height.

      The two axes are separated by staying physical:

      1. `flex-grow: 0` and `flex-basis: auto` are constant, so the main size —
         whichever axis that turns out to be — is read from `width` / `height`
         as authored rather than from a flex value that means different things
         in different parents.
      2. Every width and every height below is a REAL value, never `auto`.
         `align-items` / `align-self: stretch` only applies to a cross size of
         `auto`, so a non-auto value on both axes makes this Group immune to
         the parent's stretch in either direction. `fit-content` is what `auto`
         should have been here: same content sizing, but it cannot be stretched.
      3. `flex-shrink` is the one flex longhand still used. It is main-axis too,
         but it is benign on either: on the width it holds or yields a row
         share, on the height it only ever refuses to shrink below content.

      The result is that Width and Height each own one property and never write
      to each other, whichever way the parent happens to be pointing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    flex-grow: 0;
    flex-basis: auto;

    {% case height_mode %}
      {% when 'stretch' %}
        {%- comment -%}
          Match the tallest sibling on the flex line. `height: auto` is
          deliberate — it is the one case that OPTS IN to the parent's stretch,
          which is what "as tall as my siblings" means. It only has siblings to
          match in a row parent; in a column parent it degrades to the content
          height, and the non-auto width above still blocks the stretch from
          landing on the width instead.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        align-self: stretch;
        height: auto;
      {% when 'fill_parent' %}
        {%- comment -%}
          Take the parent's full height. `align-self: stretch` fills a row
          parent; `min-height: 100%` fills a column or block parent that has a
          real height, and is inert against an auto-height one. No `height:
          100%` — a percentage height opts the box out of stretch and then
          resolves to auto against a content-sized parent, collapsing it (the
          same trap Rich Content's panel was in).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        align-self: stretch;
        height: auto;
        min-height: 100%;
      {% else %}
        {%- comment -%}
          Auto: the natural content height, in every parent. `fit-content`
          rather than `auto` so the parent's stretch cannot inflate it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        height: fit-content;
    {% endcase %}
    --row-item-min: {{ row_item_min }}px;
    {%- comment -%}
      Space between items is the merchant's explicit choice, emitted as-is.

      It used to be multiplied by `--layout-gap-container-mobile`, which
      design-system-vars set to 0 in Minimal mode — so `calc(var(--space-sm) *
      0)` silently flattened the gap to 0px and the select did nothing at all
      in Minimal, with no hint in the editor as to why. That factor no longer
      exists; it was deleted with the alias layer on 2026-09-04. Minimal container /
      grid / carousel gap factors are a REMOVED convention (see
      docs/theme-styles.md, "Removed conventions"); spacing is meant to come
      from the resolved token contract, and Minimal flattens surfaces —
      padding, radius, borders — not a spacing value a merchant typed in.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    gap: {{ gap_css }};
    --gap-size: {{ gap_css }};
    {{ layout_css_mobile }}
  }

  .group--{{ block.id }} > * {
    min-width: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Width: sizes this Group inside a row parent. Emitted after the parent's
    `> *` rules at equal specificity, so these win; the explicit min-width: 0
    defeats the parent's min-width: var(--row-item-min). Inside a
    column-desktop parent Group the forced width: 100% !important still wins
    there — widths are meaningful in row contexts.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Per the sizing contract above, every branch writes `width` and at most
    `flex-shrink`. None of them touch `flex-grow`, `flex-basis` or
    `align-self`, so none of them can move the height in a column parent.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% case width_key %}
    {% when 'hug' %}
      .group--{{ block.id }} {
        width: fit-content;
        max-width: 100%;
        flex-shrink: 1;
        min-width: 0;
      }
    {% when 'fill' %}
      {%- comment -%}
        Share the line. A 100% basis that every sibling also asks for cannot
        fit, so the row shrinks them to equal parts — the same result the old
        `flex: 1 1 0%` gave, without spending flex-grow on an axis that may
        turn out to be the height.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      .group--{{ block.id }} {
        width: 100%;
        flex-shrink: 1;
        min-width: 0;
      }
    {% when 'full' %}
      {%- comment -%}
        Full takes the whole width of whatever wraps this Group. In a wrapping
        row it claims a line of its own: at 100% wide and unshrinkable it has
        no room to share with a sibling.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      .group--{{ block.id }} {
        width: 100%;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        min-width: 0;
      }
    {% when 'fixed' %}
      .group--{{ block.id }} {
        width: {{ block.settings.fixed_width }}px;
        max-width: 100%;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        min-width: 0;
      }
    {% when 'percent' %}
      .group--{{ block.id }} {
        width: calc({{ pw }}% - var(--gap-size, 0px) * {{ gap_factor }});
        flex-shrink: 0;
        min-width: 0;
      }
  {% endcase %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Row children default to flex: 0 1 auto, which sizes them by their own
    intrinsic content width rather than a share of available space. Any
    unconstrained content that reads its own width back from its ancestor
    (e.g. a Swiper carousel set to width:100%) can then create a growth
    feedback loop. Bound row children the same way _layout.liquid does,
    unless a child declares its own explicit flex-basis (e.g. Rich Media's
    row_width), which still wins since it's set directly on that element.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if block.settings.direction_mobile == 'row' %}
    .group--{{ block.id }} > * {
      {% if row_item_min > 0 %}
        flex: 1 1 var(--row-item-min);
        min-width: var(--row-item-min);
      {% else %}
        flex: 0 1 auto;
        min-width: 0;
      {% endif %}
    }
  {% endif %}

  @media screen and (min-width: 768px) {
    .group--{{ block.id }} {
      {%- comment -%}
        No gap override here. The two breakpoints only ever differed by the
        Minimal factor that is now gone; the space token itself is a clamp, so
        it already scales with the viewport on its own.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{ layout_css_desktop }}
    }

    {% if block.settings.direction_desktop == 'row' %}
      .group--{{ block.id }} > * {
        {% if row_item_min > 0 %}
          flex: 1 1 var(--row-item-min);
          min-width: var(--row-item-min);
        {% else %}
          flex: 0 1 auto;
          min-width: 0;
        {% endif %}
      }
    {% endif %}
    {% if block.settings.direction_desktop != 'row' %}
      {%- comment -%}
        A child may declare its own row-only width hint (e.g. Rich Media's
        row_width flex-basis, which is scoped to this same breakpoint and has
        no way to know its parent Group actually resolved to column here).
        Force full width so "column direction" is a hard invariant of this
        Group regardless of what a child assumes about its context.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      .group--{{ block.id }} > * {
        flex: 0 1 auto;
        min-width: 0;
        width: 100% !important;
      }
    {% endif %}
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div class="group--{{ block.id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Group",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Direction",
      "info": "Group stacks the blocks inside it in a row or a column. It is invisible — it adds no background, border or padding of its own. Nest Groups to build a layout; use Container when you need a padded, visible surface."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction_mobile",
      "label": "Mobile Direction",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "row",
          "label": "Row (side by side)"
        },
        {
          "value": "column",
          "label": "Column (stacked)"
        }
      ],
      "default": "column"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction_desktop",
      "label": "Desktop Direction",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "row",
          "label": "Row (side by side)"
        },
        {
          "value": "column",
          "label": "Column (stacked)"
        }
      ],
      "default": "row"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "wrap",
      "label": "Let items wrap",
      "info": "Row only: items drop onto a new line instead of squeezing.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "row_item_min_width",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 480,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Smallest item width",
      "info": "Row only: items wrap once they get narrower than this, and share the row equally. Set 0 to let each item keep its own size — use 0 for rows mixing a small fixed item (an avatar, an icon) with a flexible one.",
      "default": 240
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Alignment",
      "info": "Both alignments apply in either direction — in a row they position items across and down, in a column along and across."
    },
    {
      "type": "text_alignment",
      "id": "align_x_mobile",
      "label": "Horizontal Alignment (Mobile)",
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "text_alignment",
      "id": "align_x_desktop",
      "label": "Horizontal Alignment (Desktop)",
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align_y_mode",
      "label": "Vertical placement",
      "info": "Alignment pins items to the top, middle or bottom. Spread pushes them apart — use it to hold one group at the top and another at the bottom. Spread needs a Height other than Auto in a column.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "alignment",
          "label": "Alignment"
        },
        {
          "value": "spread",
          "label": "Spread"
        }
      ],
      "default": "alignment"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spread",
      "label": "Spread",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "space_between",
          "label": "Space between"
        },
        {
          "value": "space_around",
          "label": "Space around"
        }
      ],
      "default": "space_between",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.align_y_mode == 'spread' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align_y_mobile",
      "label": "Vertical Alignment (Mobile)",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.align_y_mode == 'alignment' }}",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "top",
          "label": "Top"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "Middle"
        },
        {
          "value": "bottom",
          "label": "Bottom"
        }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align_y_desktop",
      "label": "Vertical Alignment (Desktop)",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.align_y_mode == 'alignment' }}",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "top",
          "label": "Top"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "Middle"
        },
        {
          "value": "bottom",
          "label": "Bottom"
        }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Size"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "Space between items",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "None"
        },
        {
          "value": "xs",
          "label": "XS"
        },
        {
          "value": "sm",
          "label": "SM"
        },
        {
          "value": "md",
          "label": "MD"
        },
        {
          "value": "lg",
          "label": "LG"
        },
        {
          "value": "xl",
          "label": "XL"
        },
        {
          "value": "2xl",
          "label": "2XL"
        }
      ],
      "default": "sm"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "width_mode",
      "label": "Width",
      "info": "Auto lets the content decide. Custom sets an exact width. Applies when this Group sits beside something in a row — in a column it is always full width on desktop.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "auto",
          "label": "Auto"
        },
        {
          "value": "custom",
          "label": "Custom"
        }
      ],
      "default": "auto"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "width_auto",
      "label": "Auto Width",
      "info": "Fill takes the space left over beside its siblings. Hug shrinks to the content. Full takes the whole width of whatever wraps this Group — in a row that puts it on its own line.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "fill",
          "label": "Fill available space"
        },
        {
          "value": "hug",
          "label": "Hug content"
        },
        {
          "value": "full",
          "label": "Full width (own line)"
        }
      ],
      "default": "fill",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.width_mode == 'auto' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "width_custom",
      "label": "Custom Width",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "percent",
          "label": "Percentage"
        },
        {
          "value": "fixed",
          "label": "Fixed"
        }
      ],
      "default": "percent",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.width_mode == 'custom' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "percent_width",
      "label": "Percentage",
      "info": "Share of the row this Group takes. 100% fills the line on its own.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "25",
          "label": "25%"
        },
        {
          "value": "33",
          "label": "33%"
        },
        {
          "value": "50",
          "label": "50%"
        },
        {
          "value": "66",
          "label": "66%"
        },
        {
          "value": "75",
          "label": "75%"
        },
        {
          "value": "100",
          "label": "100%"
        }
      ],
      "default": "50",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.width_mode == 'custom' and block.settings.width_custom == 'percent' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "fixed_width",
      "min": 120,
      "max": 800,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Fixed width",
      "default": 320,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.width_mode == 'custom' and block.settings.width_custom == 'fixed' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "height_mode",
      "label": "Height",
      "info": "Auto follows the content. Stretch matches the tallest thing beside it. Fill Parent takes the parent's full height — only works when the parent already has one.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "auto",
          "label": "Auto"
        },
        {
          "value": "stretch",
          "label": "Stretch"
        },
        {
          "value": "fill_parent",
          "label": "Fill Parent"
        }
      ],
      "default": "auto"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_group"
    },
    {
      "type": "_block_items_grid"
    },
    {
      "type": "rich_content"
    },
    {
